      "nautilus t618 treadmill",
      "nautilus t616 treadmill",
      "treadmill nautilus t614",
      "nautilus treadmill recall",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Closest on Amazon: Horizon 7.0 AT", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/brands/">Brands</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buyer’s Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Nautilus Treadmills: What Happened, and What to Buy Instead</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        Nautilus treadmills — the T614, T616 and T618 — were a staple of Best Buy and Amazon listings for a decade, and they still turn up second-hand. But no Nautilus treadmill has been sold new for years, the T616 and T618 were recalled in 2022 with no remedy now available, and the Nautilus name itself was sold off in 2023. Here is what each model was, which used units to avoid, who owns what today, and the current machines from the same family tree.
      </p>

