              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T616</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Bowflex T6</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Same deck, 325 lb, $999 on sale</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T618</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Bowflex T9</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Same 350 lb rating, wider 22-inch deck</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Outside the family, the <a href="/horizon-7-0-at-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Horizon 7.0 AT</a> (also Johnson Health Tech) and the machines in our <a href="/best-treadmill-under-1000-reviews/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best treadmills under $1,000</a> and <a href="/best-folding-treadmill-reviews/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best folding treadmills</a> roundups cover the same budget.
          </p>
        </div>
